WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.190
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.460 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.330 --> 01:37.789
[Episode 44]

4
01:38.380 --> 01:41.950
[Forward Command Headquarters, Panzhou Village, Sichuan]

5
01:38.479 --> 01:41.039
I agree with the Central Committee's policy to move north.

6
01:41.039 --> 01:43.150
But Chairman Zhang's intention is very clear.

7
01:42.060 --> 01:46.259
[Xu Xiangqian, Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters and of the 4th Front Army]

8
01:43.509 --> 01:44.910
He refuses to move north.

9
01:45.070 --> 01:46.509
You and I both served under him.

10
01:46.370 --> 01:49.580
[Chen Changhao, Director of the General Political Department of Red Army; Political Commissar of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters and the 4th Front Army]

11
01:46.620 --> 01:48.620
We both belong to the 4th Front Army.

12
01:49.280 --> 01:49.840
At this time...

13
01:49.840 --> 01:51.300
Let's not talk about this.

14
01:53.860 --> 01:55.520
I think it should be like this.

15
01:55.729 --> 01:56.700
In the telegram,

16
01:56.860 --> 01:58.500
we should only start from a military perspective

17
01:58.500 --> 01:59.700
and objectively explain the pros and cons

18
01:59.700 --> 02:01.580
of moving north and south.

19
02:01.860 --> 02:03.060
We must make it clear.

20
02:06.170 --> 02:08.250
Okay, let's do as you say for now.

21
02:26.810 --> 02:27.500
Chairman.

22
02:27.620 --> 02:28.300
Chairman.

23
02:28.820 --> 02:29.500
Chairman.

24
02:32.220 --> 02:32.900
Chairman.

25
02:54.500 --> 02:55.060
Mao.

26
02:55.340 --> 02:56.400
Let's talk inside.

27
02:59.220 --> 03:00.480
How is Enlai's health?

28
03:02.300 --> 03:04.500
He still has a high fever occasionally.

29
03:04.780 --> 03:06.180
And his body is very weak.

30
03:06.650 --> 03:07.360
In addition,

31
03:07.360 --> 03:09.800
Comrade Deng Yingchao is also very sick.

32
03:10.300 --> 03:12.400
To facilitate the doctor's nursing and care,

33
03:12.400 --> 03:13.730
she moved in with Enlai.

34
03:15.850 --> 03:18.740
I don't have time to visit them right now.

35
03:18.850 --> 03:21.579
Please express my apologies to them on my behalf.

36
03:24.600 --> 03:27.310
[Peng Dehuai, Commander of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

37
03:26.500 --> 03:27.250
Mao.

38
03:27.970 --> 03:30.130
I've been hearing some troubling things

39
03:30.130 --> 03:32.930
in conversations with Fourth Front Army comrades

40
03:33.440 --> 03:34.840
these past few days.

41
03:35.970 --> 03:37.300
Zhang Guotao

42
03:40.530 --> 03:41.790
might have ambitions.

43
03:42.090 --> 03:44.350
The Central Committee has to be on guard.

44
03:46.780 --> 03:48.900
The situation is indeed complicated.

45
03:48.900 --> 03:50.570
I have already sent the 11th Regiment

46
03:50.570 --> 03:52.690
to station near your camp

47
03:52.780 --> 03:53.740
just in case.

48
03:55.650 --> 03:56.380
That's good.

49
03:56.740 --> 03:57.500
Also,

50
03:57.940 --> 04:00.220
didn't Zhang Guotao confiscate

51
04:00.220 --> 04:02.300
the cipher codes we used to communicate before?

52
04:02.300 --> 04:04.300
I had someone make a new set of codes.

53
04:04.500 --> 04:06.830
I've already sent Comrade Wu Ting to E'jie

54
04:06.970 --> 04:08.890
to deliver them to Lin Biao and Nie Rongzhen.

55
04:08.890 --> 04:11.900
You truly have a military strategist's keen insight and decisiveness.

56
04:11.900 --> 04:14.560
Mao, when you proposed at the Politburo meeting

57
04:14.650 --> 04:17.740
to restore the designation of the 1st Front Red Army,

58
04:17.779 --> 04:19.130
I thought of this.

59
04:19.769 --> 04:21.450
Please rest assured, Central Committee.

60
04:21.450 --> 04:23.010
No matter what happens,

61
04:23.210 --> 04:24.500
our 1st Front Red Army

62
04:25.190 --> 04:28.030
will stand with the CPC Central Committee.

63
04:30.490 --> 04:31.690
What is Party spirit?

64
04:32.330 --> 04:34.470
It is to uphold the leadership of the CPC Central Committee.

65
04:34.470 --> 04:36.670
This is the Party spirit of Communists.

66
04:45.280 --> 04:49.230
[E'jie, Gansu]

67
04:57.010 --> 04:57.740
Eat slowly.

68
04:59.460 --> 05:00.170
Drink some water.

69
05:00.090 --> 05:04.500
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Army, First Front Army]

70
05:05.680 --> 05:06.610
Have some water.

71
05:08.860 --> 05:10.860
Did Comrade Peng Dehuai say anything else?

72
05:10.630 --> 05:15.850
[Wu Ting, Commander of the Artillery Battalion, 3rd Army]

73
05:11.500 --> 05:12.300
No.

74
05:12.400 --> 05:13.910
He only said it was to facilitate

75
05:13.910 --> 05:16.910
communication among the troops of the 1st Front Army.

76
05:18.880 --> 05:22.550
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

77
05:20.570 --> 05:21.570
Comrade Wu Ting.

78
05:21.980 --> 05:22.960
You've worked hard.

79
05:22.960 --> 05:24.130
Get some good rest now.

80
05:24.130 --> 05:25.260
Staff Officer Fang.

81
05:25.570 --> 05:25.740
Here.

82
05:25.740 --> 05:27.060
Go see Comrade Wu Ting off.

83
05:27.060 --> 05:28.000
Arrange a room for him.

84
05:28.000 --> 05:29.010
Let him have a good rest.

85
05:29.010 --> 05:29.660
Yes.

86
05:32.340 --> 05:33.800
Comrade, this way please.

87
05:39.810 --> 05:41.300
Report, urgent telegram.

88
05:44.310 --> 05:46.060
Take this and decode it immediately.

89
05:46.060 --> 05:46.670
Yes.

90
06:07.270 --> 06:09.150
Report, it has been decoded.

91
06:18.010 --> 06:20.580
The 1st Red Army Corps should assemble at E'jie

92
06:20.580 --> 06:23.540
and send a team to Luoda for reconnaissance.

93
06:24.370 --> 06:25.100
Zhou Enlai,

94
06:25.330 --> 06:26.180
Peng Dehuai,

95
06:26.330 --> 06:27.300
and Li Fuchun.

96
06:27.980 --> 06:29.300
This is inconsistent with the previous orders

97
06:29.300 --> 06:31.230
from the Frontline Headquarters.

98
06:31.500 --> 06:33.060
Since it was signed by Vice Chairman Zhou,

99
06:33.060 --> 06:34.520
we will execute the order.

100
06:36.770 --> 06:38.330
Send another telegram to Comrade Peng Dehuai

101
06:38.330 --> 06:39.200
to ask for details.

102
06:39.200 --> 06:39.740
Yes.

103
06:49.050 --> 06:51.380
[Axi, Yanong Village, Sichuan]

104
06:59.210 --> 07:01.910
[Deng Yingchao, Committee Member of the Party General Branch of the Cadre Rest-and-Rehabilitation Company]

105
07:11.570 --> 07:14.370
Ms. Deng, your medicine is ready.

106
07:15.230 --> 07:16.210
I'll be right outside.

107
07:16.210 --> 07:17.540
Call me if you need anything.

108
07:17.540 --> 07:19.180
Thank you, Comrade Jin Biao.

109
07:19.690 --> 07:20.540
Thanks for your hard work.

110
07:20.540 --> 07:21.420
It's no trouble.

111
07:21.420 --> 07:22.420
I'll go out first.

112
08:42.210 --> 08:43.539
Comrade Wu Hao,

113
08:44.940 --> 08:49.370
thank you for pulling through.

114
09:12.060 --> 09:13.090
Chao.

115
09:17.900 --> 09:19.260
Comrade Yihao.

116
09:22.070 --> 09:25.510
Your observation skills are still not up to par.

117
09:27.780 --> 09:30.020
When you pulled my beard just now,

118
09:30.210 --> 09:31.860
I was already awake.

119
09:44.060 --> 09:45.660
I didn't need to open my eyes

120
09:46.180 --> 09:50.110
to know the look in your eyes.

121
09:51.660 --> 09:54.300
When we got married in 1925,

122
09:55.540 --> 09:57.340
you came to Guangzhou to find me.

123
09:58.470 --> 10:01.710
I was busy with the Canton-Hong Kong strike.

124
10:02.680 --> 10:05.040
We hadn't seen each other for five years.

125
10:07.030 --> 10:09.380
Chen Geng brought you to see me.

126
10:11.060 --> 10:12.810
We were separated by the crowd,

127
10:13.490 --> 10:15.330
less than twenty meters apart.

128
10:15.810 --> 10:17.570
The look in your eyes

129
10:18.140 --> 10:20.330
has always been engraved in my heart.

130
10:21.810 --> 10:23.780
In my most difficult times,

131
10:24.810 --> 10:26.570
it has always inspired me.

132
10:28.060 --> 10:29.660
You just said

133
10:30.410 --> 10:33.900
you were grateful to me for pulling through.

134
10:35.110 --> 10:36.420
In the grasslands,

135
10:36.960 --> 10:41.030
you saved the last anti-inflammatory injection for me.

136
10:42.830 --> 10:44.240
I know you.

137
10:45.660 --> 10:47.900
If any comrade needed it,

138
10:48.760 --> 10:50.970
you would have given it to them too.

139
10:52.450 --> 10:53.780
I also know

140
10:54.450 --> 10:56.380
that when you fell into the swamp,

141
10:57.260 --> 10:59.490
it was the comrades who saved you.

142
11:01.210 --> 11:02.260
Chao,

143
11:03.730 --> 11:05.490
thank you

144
11:06.960 --> 11:08.320
for pulling through.

145
11:19.850 --> 11:21.420
When I was in Liping,

146
11:22.790 --> 11:25.380
I learned two Dong songs.

147
11:31.290 --> 11:33.050
There was one

148
11:33.780 --> 11:35.730
I wanted to sing to you.

149
11:36.180 --> 11:39.970
But I was so tired then

150
11:40.240 --> 11:42.750
that I actually fell asleep in the yard.

151
11:43.270 --> 11:45.480
Can I sing it to you now?

152
11:49.490 --> 11:50.850
Comrade Yihao.

153
11:51.610 --> 11:54.490
If you fall asleep now,

154
11:55.570 --> 11:57.810
then consider this song

155
11:58.160 --> 12:05.110
as a lullaby for your dreams.

156
12:09.210 --> 12:21.560
Everyone, listen as I sing.

157
12:23.690 --> 12:36.210
We Dong folks love many things.

158
12:37.670 --> 12:50.550
We act, we sing, and speak with flair.

159
12:51.090 --> 13:04.020
Glutinous rice keeps us strong and healthy.

160
13:04.660 --> 13:16.780
Everyone, listen as I sing.

161
13:18.330 --> 13:31.020
We Dong folks love many things.

162
14:17.330 --> 14:18.210
Chairman Mao.

163
14:18.450 --> 14:19.730
This is the telegram Xiangqian and I

164
14:19.730 --> 14:21.530
jointly sent to Chairman Zhang.

165
14:23.900 --> 14:25.540
We have said what needs to be said.

166
14:25.540 --> 14:28.740
Everything still depends on Chairman Zhang's decision.

167
14:30.450 --> 14:31.510
Comrade Changhao.

168
14:31.660 --> 14:33.210
Going north to resist Japanese aggression

169
14:33.210 --> 14:35.690
is a major event that determines the fate of the Party and the Red Army.

170
14:35.690 --> 14:38.750
Individuals must obey the organization's decisions.

171
14:39.090 --> 14:40.060
I suggest

172
14:40.870 --> 14:43.000
we hold an informal Politburo meeting

173
14:44.450 --> 14:46.710
and invite Comrade Xiangqian to join us.

174
14:46.810 --> 14:48.090
After unifying our thoughts,

175
14:48.090 --> 14:50.490
we will jointly send a telegram to the Left Route Army,

176
14:50.490 --> 14:52.750
asking them to march north immediately.

177
14:52.900 --> 14:53.780
I agree.

178
14:54.690 --> 14:55.170
Okay.

179
14:55.850 --> 14:57.210
When and where will it be held?

180
14:57.210 --> 14:58.670
I'll go inform Xiangqian.

181
15:03.060 --> 15:04.180
Comrade Enlai

182
15:04.320 --> 15:06.200
is in poor health and has difficulty moving.

183
15:06.200 --> 15:08.260
Let's hold the meeting at his residence.

184
15:08.260 --> 15:09.420
Let's schedule it

185
15:09.850 --> 15:11.310
for after dinner tonight.

186
15:11.540 --> 15:12.180
Okay.

187
15:12.490 --> 15:14.730
All right, I'll go tell Xiangqian.

188
15:19.330 --> 15:21.210
Judging from the content of the telegram,

189
15:21.210 --> 15:22.180
the words of Xu and Chen

190
15:22.180 --> 15:23.380
are quite sincere.

191
15:23.610 --> 15:24.900
With their support,

192
15:25.020 --> 15:26.510
this matter will be much easier to handle.

193
15:26.510 --> 15:28.450
I'm not too worried about Xiangqian.

194
15:28.450 --> 15:30.330
He had already expressed his support for marching north

195
15:30.330 --> 15:33.490
to Shaanxi and Gansu at the Maogong meeting.

196
15:33.690 --> 15:34.810
In the subsequent meetings,

197
15:34.810 --> 15:36.900
he also agreed with the Central Committee's policy.

198
15:36.900 --> 15:39.060
But Comrade Changhao

199
15:39.260 --> 15:40.990
seems to have some hesitation.

200
15:42.450 --> 15:43.780
What makes you say that?

201
15:45.210 --> 15:46.870
Although the telegram states that

202
15:46.870 --> 15:47.810
marching north is the best course

203
15:47.810 --> 15:49.140
and moving south the lesser option,

204
15:49.140 --> 15:50.140
it also says,

205
15:50.330 --> 15:52.860
"If the Left Route Army cannot advance north,

206
15:53.270 --> 15:56.200
we will have no choice but to take the lesser option."

207
16:07.810 --> 16:09.020
I know Xiangqian.

208
16:09.900 --> 16:13.900
[Zhang Guotao, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo, Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission, and Political Commissar-General of the Red Army]

209
16:10.090 --> 16:11.810
He is a military cadre

210
16:12.090 --> 16:14.330
without so many political thoughts in his head.

211
16:14.060 --> 16:16.790
[Huang Chao, Secretary-General of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission and the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Soviet Government]

212
16:15.020 --> 16:16.610
As for Changhao,

213
16:17.260 --> 16:18.330
I believe

214
16:18.810 --> 16:21.410
he will stand by my side at the critical moment.

215
16:21.450 --> 16:23.480
But the telegram also emphasized

216
16:24.420 --> 16:26.940
that marching north is the best plan.

217
16:33.660 --> 16:35.610
Strength determines everything.

218
16:36.210 --> 16:38.060
I have no intention of debating

219
16:38.090 --> 16:39.750
what's the best or worst plan.

220
16:40.330 --> 16:43.330
If we can't settle this through reasoned discussion,

221
16:43.450 --> 16:46.710
then let's speak plainly and put all our cards on the table.

222
16:53.100 --> 16:57.120
[10:00 p.m., September 8, 1935]

223
16:55.210 --> 16:55.970
Comrades.

224
16:57.260 --> 17:00.760
[Yanong, Shaanxi] [Informal Meeting of the CPC Politburo]

225
16:57.490 --> 17:02.020
I want to formally express my view.

226
17:03.700 --> 17:04.560
Marching north

227
17:05.380 --> 17:07.579
is not only a strategic consideration,

228
17:08.099 --> 17:11.099
but also represents the direction of our revolution.

229
17:11.420 --> 17:13.339
Japan has pushed deep into North China

230
17:13.339 --> 17:15.740
and is becoming increasingly aggressive.

231
17:16.420 --> 17:18.140
As the Communist Party of China

232
17:18.140 --> 17:21.010
and the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army under its leadership,

233
17:21.010 --> 17:23.400
we must never evade or run away.

234
17:23.970 --> 17:26.290
We must never break our promise to the people

235
17:26.290 --> 17:27.839
or detach ourselves from the masses.

236
17:27.839 --> 17:31.290
A Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army far from the anti-Japanese frontline

237
17:31.290 --> 17:33.260
will surely be like water without a source

238
17:33.260 --> 17:34.690
and won't go far.

239
17:35.890 --> 17:39.130
This is the telegram that Comrade Zedong and I

240
17:39.580 --> 17:40.740
prepared this afternoon for Zhang, Zhu, and Liu

241
17:40.740 --> 17:43.500
of the Left Route Army.

242
17:43.560 --> 17:44.520
The main content

243
17:44.610 --> 17:46.690
is to reiterate to them

244
17:46.900 --> 17:48.620
the various disadvantages of marching south

245
17:48.620 --> 17:51.010
and persuade them to march north as soon as possible.

246
17:51.010 --> 17:52.670
Everyone, please take a look.

247
17:53.270 --> 17:54.940
If there are no objections,

248
17:55.460 --> 17:57.660
I will send the telegram to them

249
17:57.820 --> 17:59.420
in the name of the seven of us.

250
18:41.900 --> 18:42.880
Comrade Enlai.

251
18:45.290 --> 18:45.860
Okay.

252
18:50.900 --> 18:53.730
Everyone can express their opinions.

253
18:54.250 --> 18:54.940
I agree.

254
18:55.050 --> 18:55.900
Me too.

255
18:56.180 --> 18:57.100
I agree.

256
19:00.860 --> 19:02.290
I agree with the Central Committee.

257
19:02.290 --> 19:04.750
The two armies should march north together.

258
19:15.820 --> 19:17.420
I agree to send the telegram,

259
19:17.450 --> 19:20.380
striving for the two armies to march north together.

260
19:20.860 --> 19:21.770
However...

261
19:23.050 --> 19:24.110
Comrade Changhao,

262
19:24.620 --> 19:27.550
feel free to speak your mind if you have any concerns.

263
19:27.900 --> 19:29.300
If marching north fails,

264
19:29.690 --> 19:32.620
can the Central Committee consider marching south,

265
19:32.930 --> 19:36.130
or perhaps explore a compromise?

266
19:36.770 --> 19:37.830
Comrade Changhao,

267
19:39.490 --> 19:41.050
marching north and marching south

268
19:41.050 --> 19:43.250
are two completely different strategic guidelines.

269
19:43.250 --> 19:45.580
There is no compromise.

270
19:45.970 --> 19:49.830
The Central Committee will definitely not consider marching south.

271
19:51.620 --> 19:52.980
I have nothing further to add.

272
19:52.980 --> 19:56.170
Okay, I'll arrange to send the telegram immediately.

273
20:13.550 --> 20:16.450
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters]

274
20:20.180 --> 20:20.910
You're back.

275
20:22.540 --> 20:22.770
Come.

276
20:22.770 --> 20:24.100
You haven't rested yet?

277
20:24.180 --> 20:25.440
Have some water first.

278
20:27.530 --> 20:28.290
Okay.

279
20:28.490 --> 20:29.620
How was the meeting?

280
20:30.570 --> 20:33.700
The Central Committee still insists on marching north.

281
20:33.800 --> 20:34.860
Comrade Jianying,

282
20:35.410 --> 20:37.610
what's your opinion on marching north?

283
20:39.820 --> 20:40.690
You two

284
20:41.010 --> 20:41.770
are the Political Commissar-General

285
20:41.770 --> 20:43.430
and the Commander-in-Chief.

286
20:43.580 --> 20:44.780
As the Chief of Staff,

287
20:44.840 --> 20:46.180
I'll follow the Central Committee's decision,

288
20:46.180 --> 20:47.220
just as you do.

289
20:54.180 --> 20:55.240
It's getting late.

290
20:55.290 --> 20:56.210
Let's all rest.

291
20:58.120 --> 20:58.770
Okay.

292
21:47.230 --> 21:49.810
[September 9, 1935]

293
21:57.970 --> 21:58.900
Comrade Zedong.

294
21:58.970 --> 22:00.170
Zhang Guotao's reply

295
22:00.420 --> 22:01.860
refuted our policy of marching north

296
22:01.860 --> 22:03.530
point by point.

297
22:04.050 --> 22:07.230
It seems that no matter how hard the Central Committee tries,

298
22:07.230 --> 22:08.790
he just won't listen.

299
22:09.420 --> 22:10.780
We are all Party members.

300
22:10.780 --> 22:12.110
But we are so different.

301
22:12.450 --> 22:13.730
Before the Zunyi Conference,

302
22:13.730 --> 22:15.810
even though you

303
22:16.050 --> 22:17.380
and Comrade Peng Dehuai

304
22:17.380 --> 22:18.580
had objections to the command

305
22:18.580 --> 22:19.840
of Comrade Li De and me,

306
22:20.210 --> 22:22.010
we were all open and aboveboard.

307
22:22.010 --> 22:22.730
Even when we argued,

308
22:22.730 --> 22:24.100
we did so openly.

309
22:24.340 --> 22:25.380
Now Zhang Guotao,

310
22:25.530 --> 22:28.010
is using his numerical and military strength

311
22:28.010 --> 22:30.050
to feigns compliance with the Central Committee

312
22:30.050 --> 22:31.210
and acts willfully.

313
22:31.660 --> 22:32.590
Comrade Zedong,

314
22:32.730 --> 22:35.050
what should we do in this situation?

315
22:37.780 --> 22:39.890
Whether to march north or south

316
22:40.530 --> 22:41.820
is not a matter of each side

317
22:41.820 --> 22:43.120
having its own justification.

318
22:43.120 --> 22:45.120
It's a question of principle.

319
22:45.200 --> 22:47.200
There is no room for bargaining.

320
22:49.820 --> 22:51.680
It concerns our future and destiny.

321
22:51.680 --> 22:53.900
Even if the Red Army has only one soldier left,

322
22:53.900 --> 22:56.300
we must go to the anti-Japanese frontline.

323
22:57.580 --> 22:58.430
I said it before.

324
22:58.430 --> 23:00.530
A single spark can start a prairie fire.

325
23:00.530 --> 23:01.340
If we have no men,

326
23:01.340 --> 23:02.210
we can get men.

327
23:02.660 --> 23:03.580
If we have no guns,

328
23:03.580 --> 23:04.500
we can get guns.

329
23:07.590 --> 23:10.190
Just as Zhang Guotao openly split the Red Army,

330
23:10.220 --> 23:11.330
opposing the march north

331
23:11.330 --> 23:13.260
and ordering a southward advance,

332
23:13.700 --> 23:15.360
the 25th Army, marching north

333
23:15.690 --> 23:17.530
thousands of li away in northern Shaanxi,

334
23:17.530 --> 23:19.620
arrived in Bao'an County.

335
23:19.990 --> 23:21.270
At Baozichuan,

336
23:21.290 --> 23:24.050
it held a meeting of the CPC Shaanxi-Gansu Border Provincial Committee,

337
23:24.050 --> 23:26.050
which decided to appoint Cheng Zihua

338
23:26.050 --> 23:28.900
as acting secretary of the CPC Shaanxi-Gansu Border Provincial Committee

339
23:28.900 --> 23:31.210
and Political Commissar of the 25th Army.

340
23:30.890 --> 23:34.740
[Mount Yongning, Bao'an County, Shaanxi]

341
23:31.690 --> 23:34.840
Xu Haidong as Commander of the 25th Army.

342
23:35.210 --> 23:37.990
They also made political mobilization for entering the Shaanxi and Gansu Revolutionary Base Area

343
23:37.990 --> 23:41.230
and joining forces with the Shaanxi and Gansu Red Army.

344
23:45.820 --> 23:48.690
[Xi Zhongxun, Chairman of the Soviet Government of the Shaanxi-Gansu Border Region]

345
23:46.900 --> 23:47.970
The 25th Red Army is here!

346
23:47.970 --> 23:48.510
They are here!

347
23:48.510 --> 23:49.270
Let's go!

348
23:50.730 --> 23:51.180
Go!

349
23:51.620 --> 23:52.050
Go.

350
23:53.630 --> 23:55.680
[Xu Haidong, Commander of 25th Red Army]

351
23:54.410 --> 23:56.210
Zi Hua, look!

352
23:55.730 --> 23:58.780
[Cheng Zihua, Political Commissar of the 25th Red Army]

353
23:59.290 --> 24:00.290
Comrades,

354
24:00.620 --> 24:03.620
the Red Army of northern Shaanxi is here to welcome us.

355
24:03.620 --> 24:04.490
Hurry up!

356
24:11.140 --> 24:11.970
Comrade.

357
24:12.360 --> 24:13.890
Who is Comrade Cheng Zihua?

358
24:14.100 --> 24:15.450
Who is Comrade Xu Haidong?

359
24:15.450 --> 24:16.820
I am Cheng Zihua.

360
24:17.060 --> 24:19.010
This is Comrade Xu Haidong.

361
24:19.620 --> 24:20.820
We've been waiting for you.

362
24:20.820 --> 24:23.140
I am the Chairman of the Shaanxi-Gansu Border Region Soviet Government,

363
24:23.140 --> 24:23.940
Xi Zhongxun.

364
24:24.340 --> 24:25.620
I heard you arrived in northern Shaanxi,

365
24:25.620 --> 24:26.860
so I waited for you here.

366
24:26.860 --> 24:27.950
Comrade Xi Zhongxun,

367
24:27.950 --> 24:29.150
we finally found you.

368
24:29.300 --> 24:30.830
Your Long March is amazing.

369
24:31.050 --> 24:33.380
The soldiers of our 25th Red Army are so young.

370
24:33.380 --> 24:34.580
Many of them look like

371
24:34.750 --> 24:36.140
teenagers.

372
24:37.010 --> 24:38.820
You, the Chairman, are also very young.

373
24:38.820 --> 24:41.010
By the way, where is Comrade Liu Zhidan?

374
24:41.010 --> 24:43.290
He led the 26th and 27th Red Armies

375
24:43.340 --> 24:45.150
to advance to Yongping Town ahead,

376
24:45.150 --> 24:46.620
preparing to join forces with you there.

377
24:46.620 --> 24:47.050
Well,

378
24:47.140 --> 24:48.270
let's set off quickly too.

379
24:48.270 --> 24:49.900
As for the situation in the Shaanxi and Gansu region,

380
24:49.900 --> 24:51.490
I'll explain it to you on the way.

381
24:51.490 --> 24:52.420
-Okay. -Okay.

382
24:52.970 --> 24:55.530
Comrades, let's go to Yongping Town now

383
24:55.620 --> 24:57.490
to join forces with the Northern Shaanxi Red Army.

384
24:57.490 --> 24:58.360
Let's go!

385
25:54.530 --> 25:55.190
Is Mao here?

386
25:55.380 --> 25:55.970
He's inside.

387
25:55.970 --> 25:56.420
Okay.

388
25:58.380 --> 25:59.180
Mao.

389
25:59.690 --> 26:00.860
I just went to the Front Headquarters.

390
26:00.860 --> 26:03.340
I heard Chen Changhao holding a meeting from afar.

391
26:03.340 --> 26:04.210
His tone has changed,

392
26:04.210 --> 26:06.660
talking a lot about the benefits of going south.

393
26:06.660 --> 26:07.880
The root of the problem lies with Zhang Guotao.

394
26:07.880 --> 26:09.410
The situation is critical.

395
26:09.860 --> 26:11.580
We have to be on guard.

396
26:12.210 --> 26:13.560
I'll ask you just one question:

397
26:13.560 --> 26:16.540
Can we take hostages in a critical moment?

398
26:24.580 --> 26:25.380
No.

399
26:25.970 --> 26:27.030
We are the Red Army,

400
26:27.210 --> 26:28.180
not warlords.

401
26:28.420 --> 26:31.210
Taking hostages won't solve the problem.

402
26:31.580 --> 26:33.140
It will only intensify the conflict.

403
26:33.140 --> 26:35.230
I'm afraid the Central Committee's good intentions

404
26:35.230 --> 26:38.290
will fall prey to Zhang Guotao's underhanded tactics.

405
26:44.970 --> 26:45.820
Chairman Mao.

406
26:46.100 --> 26:49.500
This is the telegram Zhang Guotao just sent to Chen Changhao.

407
27:01.210 --> 27:03.340
Did Chen Changhao see this telegram?

408
27:03.340 --> 27:04.210
He is speaking

409
27:04.260 --> 27:06.120
and hasn't had time to read it yet.

410
27:14.700 --> 27:15.500
Go back first.

411
27:16.120 --> 27:17.620
Don't attract his attention.

412
27:17.620 --> 27:18.290
Okay.

413
27:22.180 --> 27:22.770
Peng.

414
27:24.350 --> 27:26.270
Go get Jiaxiang, Luofu,

415
27:26.580 --> 27:27.450
and Comrade Bo Gu

416
27:27.450 --> 27:28.530
to come and discuss.

417
27:28.530 --> 27:29.140
Okay.

418
27:40.380 --> 27:41.210
It seems

419
27:41.560 --> 27:44.050
not only is the Left Route Army unable to go north,

420
27:44.050 --> 27:46.340
but we also have to face the reality that

421
27:46.570 --> 27:49.100
the 4th Front Army in the Right Route Army is going south.

422
27:49.100 --> 27:50.010
Not only that.

423
27:50.620 --> 27:52.150
The most dangerous thing is

424
27:52.290 --> 27:54.750
that the two armies are very likely to clash.

425
27:58.860 --> 27:59.970
What should we do now,

426
27:59.970 --> 28:00.900
Comrade Zedong?

427
28:01.010 --> 28:02.140
He wants to go south.

428
28:02.580 --> 28:03.770
What should we do?

429
28:03.970 --> 28:06.630
Should we just stop going north to resist Japan?

430
28:07.380 --> 28:08.200
Since he is determined to go south,

431
28:08.200 --> 28:10.250
we have no choice but to take the 1st Front Army

432
28:10.250 --> 28:11.310
and go north alone.

433
28:13.870 --> 28:16.770
Zhang Guotao won't turn back until he hits a brick wall.

434
28:16.770 --> 28:17.700
And once he does,

435
28:18.380 --> 28:19.780
he will have to turn back.

436
28:20.420 --> 28:21.770
As Han Feizi says,

437
28:21.820 --> 28:23.770
"Relying on others is no better than relying on yourself."

438
28:23.770 --> 28:24.690
At present,

439
28:25.210 --> 28:28.340
going north alone is the best way.

440
28:28.730 --> 28:30.690
Otherwise, if the Central Committee tries to persuade them again,

441
28:30.690 --> 28:31.770
a quarrel is inevitable.

442
28:31.770 --> 28:33.580
It might even lead to a conflict.

443
28:35.380 --> 28:36.250
No matter what,

444
28:36.420 --> 28:38.330
the two armies must never clash.

445
28:40.380 --> 28:42.250
I'll go to the Frontline Headquarters again

446
28:42.250 --> 28:44.180
to confirm Xu and Chen's attitude.

447
28:44.620 --> 28:45.140
Comrade Zedong.

448
28:45.140 --> 28:46.610
Mao, you can't go.

449
28:46.770 --> 28:47.750
It's too dangerous.

450
28:47.750 --> 28:49.660
You absolutely cannot go at this time.

451
28:49.660 --> 28:51.930
It's more dangerous not to go.

452
28:54.180 --> 28:54.800
Mao.

453
30:29.140 --> 30:31.320
We must learn from our previous lessons.

454
30:31.320 --> 30:32.530
The collection of grain

455
30:32.530 --> 30:33.730
must be done well.

456
30:34.050 --> 30:35.660
All units must also keep warm.

457
30:35.660 --> 30:36.820
The temperature difference in the grasslands

458
30:36.820 --> 30:37.690
is terrifying.

459
30:38.180 --> 30:39.770
Last time we crossed the grasslands,

460
30:39.770 --> 30:40.290
many comrades,

461
30:40.290 --> 30:40.970
Chairman Mao.

462
30:40.970 --> 30:41.730
all died from

463
30:42.050 --> 30:42.690
the cold.

464
30:46.250 --> 30:47.380
Comrade Xiangqian.

465
30:48.250 --> 30:50.780
Comrade Zhang Guotao has decided to go south.

466
30:51.490 --> 30:54.250
I want to hear your opinion.

467
30:56.180 --> 30:57.010
Chairman Mao.

468
30:57.450 --> 30:59.050
Since the two armies have joined forces,

469
30:59.050 --> 31:00.940
it's not appropriate to separate them again.

470
31:00.940 --> 31:02.120
As for the 4th Front Army,

471
31:02.120 --> 31:03.850
if it's divided into two parts,

472
31:03.990 --> 31:05.650
that wouldn't be good either.

473
31:09.580 --> 31:10.380
Understood.

474
31:10.900 --> 31:12.360
Is Comrade Changhao here?

475
31:12.450 --> 31:13.450
He's in a meeting.

476
31:14.160 --> 31:15.160
So this time,

477
31:15.450 --> 31:18.010
we must strive to cross the grasslands within six days.

478
31:18.010 --> 31:19.210
We must never again suffer

479
31:19.210 --> 31:20.490
the hardships, casualties, and losses we endured

480
31:20.490 --> 31:21.960
during our last crossing

481
31:21.990 --> 31:24.390
-of the grasslands... -Comrade Changhao.

482
31:24.900 --> 31:25.700
Chairman Mao.

483
31:25.860 --> 31:26.660
Are you busy?

484
31:27.690 --> 31:28.660
You go back first.

485
31:28.660 --> 31:29.730
Yes.

486
31:37.660 --> 31:40.020
Chairman Mao, do you need me?

487
31:42.620 --> 31:44.550
Regarding Comrade Zhang Guotao's

488
31:44.620 --> 31:45.940
decision to go south,

489
31:47.210 --> 31:48.860
I want to hear your opinion.

490
31:50.690 --> 31:53.450
Chairman Zhang's telegram made it very clear

491
31:54.380 --> 31:55.710
that we should go south.

492
31:56.480 --> 31:59.480
He is the General Political Commissar of the Red Army.

493
32:05.820 --> 32:06.680
All right then.

494
32:07.380 --> 32:08.620
Since we are going south,

495
32:08.620 --> 32:09.490
Luofu and a few of us

496
32:09.490 --> 32:11.420
will go find Comrade Enlai tonight

497
32:11.510 --> 32:12.460
to hold a meeting

498
32:12.970 --> 32:13.940
and discuss it.

499
32:14.150 --> 32:17.100
Comrade Enlai is entrusted by the CPC Central Committee

500
32:17.100 --> 32:18.420
as the Standing Committee member

501
32:18.420 --> 32:20.520
who makes the final decisions on military issues.

502
32:20.520 --> 32:21.920
So your personal opinion

503
32:22.180 --> 32:23.040
is that you agree to go south?

504
32:23.040 --> 32:24.570
We still need to discuss it.

505
32:25.490 --> 32:28.100
Don't assume the journey will be easy just because the descent has begun.

506
32:28.100 --> 32:31.430
Travelers are often deceived by that false sense of relief.

507
32:43.660 --> 32:44.320
Xiangqian.

508
32:44.740 --> 32:47.580
Things might be simpler than we thought.

509
32:47.770 --> 32:48.630
Let's go inside

510
32:48.710 --> 32:50.840
and discuss the specific route south.

511
33:06.530 --> 33:07.460
Comrade Zedong.

512
33:07.580 --> 33:09.240
Comrade Zedong, how did it go?

513
33:09.890 --> 33:10.890
As expected.

514
33:12.290 --> 33:13.620
We will set off right now

515
33:14.120 --> 33:15.690
to have a meeting at Enlai's place

516
33:15.690 --> 33:16.820
and study the plan to go north.

517
33:16.820 --> 33:17.820
Good, good, good.

518
33:17.970 --> 33:18.620
Leaders,

519
33:19.260 --> 33:21.460
have you figured out a countermeasure?

520
33:24.010 --> 33:24.780
Jianying.

521
33:26.730 --> 33:27.620
We plan

522
33:28.530 --> 33:30.940
to take the 1st Front Army north alone.

523
33:31.250 --> 33:32.210
Comrade Jianying,

524
33:32.210 --> 33:33.210
you have to come with us.

525
33:33.210 --> 33:34.310
You can't stay behind.

526
33:34.310 --> 33:35.030
Yes.

527
33:35.090 --> 33:35.920
Once we leave,

528
33:36.100 --> 33:38.450
Chen Changhao will suspect you first.

529
33:38.730 --> 33:40.580
Of course I want to go with the Central Committee.

530
33:40.580 --> 33:41.420
But,

531
33:42.660 --> 33:43.730
if I leave now,

532
33:44.290 --> 33:46.290
I'm afraid none of us will be able to leave.

533
33:46.290 --> 33:47.940
The Central Committee's directly subordinate units are all here now,

534
33:47.940 --> 33:49.660
especially the Second Bureau.

535
33:49.660 --> 33:50.520
Even if I leave,

536
33:51.450 --> 33:55.650
I have to take the Central Committee's directly subordinate units with me.

537
33:57.660 --> 33:58.720
Comrade Jianying,

538
33:58.860 --> 34:00.730
you are clear-headed in the face of major events.

539
34:00.730 --> 34:02.620
Okay, you must be careful.

540
34:02.940 --> 34:04.580
We will wait for you to rejoin us.

541
34:04.580 --> 34:06.580
Please rest assured, Chairman Mao.

542
34:06.820 --> 34:08.550
Please rest assured, leaders.

543
34:18.820 --> 34:19.530
Let's go.

544
34:25.090 --> 34:26.050
For now, it seems

545
34:26.420 --> 34:29.280
we still have no choice but to cross the grasslands.

546
34:31.010 --> 34:33.139
Crossing the grasslands isn't scary.

547
34:34.090 --> 34:36.610
The most important thing is to have enough food.

548
34:36.610 --> 34:38.610
We've already suffered a loss once.

549
34:38.820 --> 34:40.480
We can't suffer a second time.

550
34:41.159 --> 34:43.690
Do you have any good ideas, Comrade Jianying?

551
34:44.610 --> 34:45.969
Nothing clever.

552
34:46.449 --> 34:48.179
But I do have one foolproof way.

553
34:49.610 --> 34:50.610
Tell us.

554
34:51.050 --> 34:52.760
I'll organize cadres and soldiers

555
34:52.760 --> 34:53.840
from the Central Committee's directly subordinate units

556
34:53.840 --> 34:55.650
into small groups to gather grain,

557
34:55.650 --> 34:56.790
going from house to house

558
34:56.790 --> 34:59.100
in every village to ask for food or buy it.

559
34:59.420 --> 35:00.420
This time,

560
35:00.440 --> 35:03.170
we must prepare at least ten days' worth of grain.

561
35:04.680 --> 35:06.840
It seems this is the only way for now.

562
35:07.380 --> 35:09.300
Time is tight right now.

563
35:09.570 --> 35:12.010
The sooner this is done, the better.

564
35:15.910 --> 35:17.340
Then I will set off tonight.

565
35:17.340 --> 35:18.220
I'll go notify

566
35:18.240 --> 35:19.570
the comrades of our units now.

567
35:19.570 --> 35:20.260
Okay.

568
35:21.550 --> 35:23.150
Thank you for your hard work.

569
35:28.080 --> 35:31.210
[8:00 p.m., September 9, 1935]

570
35:30.210 --> 35:32.340
Since no one objects to the Central Committee

571
35:32.340 --> 35:34.420
taking the 1st Front Army north

572
35:34.490 --> 35:35.420
on its own,

573
35:35.740 --> 35:37.900
let's work out everyone's

574
35:37.900 --> 35:38.940
respective responsibilities.

575
35:38.940 --> 35:39.700
First,

576
35:40.010 --> 35:41.650
Comrade Mao Zedong

577
35:42.090 --> 35:43.420
will draft a Statement of

578
35:43.420 --> 35:47.130
the CPC Central Committee to Comrades on Implementing the Policy of Marching North,

579
35:47.130 --> 35:48.860
setting out the Central Committee's position

580
35:48.860 --> 35:49.900
and declaring that

581
35:49.900 --> 35:52.430
the Right Route Army will be under the command

582
35:52.610 --> 35:55.170
of Zhou Enlai, Vice Chairman of the Military Commission.

583
35:55.170 --> 35:55.820
Second,

584
35:55.970 --> 35:57.820
use the 3rd Army's radio

585
35:57.970 --> 35:59.230
to contact the 1st Army

586
35:59.570 --> 36:00.860
and have them wait at E'jie

587
36:00.860 --> 36:03.220
for the Central Committee to advance north.

588
36:03.220 --> 36:03.900
Third,

589
36:04.010 --> 36:04.650
I will contact

590
36:04.650 --> 36:06.490
Comrade Li Weihan, the Director of the Local Work Department

591
36:06.490 --> 36:07.740
of the General Political Department,

592
36:07.740 --> 36:09.340
and have him send someone to Banyou

593
36:09.340 --> 36:11.080
to inform Kaifeng and Lin Boqu

594
36:11.530 --> 36:14.530
to organize the Central Committee, government offices,

595
36:14.530 --> 36:18.190
and General Political Department stationed there to move north.

596
36:18.220 --> 36:18.900
Fourth,

597
36:19.220 --> 36:21.900
Comrade Bo Gu will contact Li De

598
36:22.060 --> 36:24.010
and have him convey the Central Committee's decision

599
36:24.010 --> 36:25.780
to march north to the Red Army University.

600
36:25.780 --> 36:28.570
Comrades Liu Shaoqi and Mo Wenhua will be tasked

601
36:28.820 --> 36:31.430
with leading all personnel of the Red Army University north.

602
36:31.430 --> 36:32.200
No problem.

603
36:32.470 --> 36:33.110
Peng,

604
36:33.840 --> 36:35.500
you need to arrange a regiment

605
36:35.670 --> 36:37.800
to protect the CPC Central Committee.

606
36:38.060 --> 36:39.300
It's already arranged.

607
36:39.300 --> 36:41.280
Chief of Staff Comrade Xiao Jinguang

608
36:41.280 --> 36:42.810
will lead the 10th Regiment

609
36:42.820 --> 36:44.720
to protect the Central Committee.

610
36:44.720 --> 36:45.850
If there are no problems,

611
36:45.850 --> 36:47.110
let's act separately.

612
36:47.610 --> 36:48.220
Remember,

613
36:48.360 --> 36:49.720
we'll set out

614
36:49.970 --> 36:52.220
at 2:00 a.m.

615
36:52.620 --> 36:55.860
All units are to say publicly that we're going out to gather grain.

616
36:55.860 --> 36:56.530
Okay, okay.

617
37:05.930 --> 37:06.580
Come.

618
37:07.530 --> 37:08.130
Come.

619
37:09.920 --> 37:10.650
Enlai,

620
37:11.310 --> 37:12.060
go rest.

621
37:12.080 --> 37:13.080
You go rest.

622
37:13.170 --> 37:14.630
I'll grind the ink for you.

623
37:22.110 --> 37:27.940
[E'jie, Gansu] [1st Army Headquarters]

624
37:25.920 --> 37:28.920
Report, urgent telegram from the Central Committee.

625
37:36.810 --> 37:39.320
The Central Committee says the course of action has changed,

626
37:39.320 --> 37:40.720
and asks us to stand by.

627
37:41.080 --> 37:43.140
Something major must have happened.

628
37:47.450 --> 37:48.420
This is Lin Biao.

629
37:48.440 --> 37:49.250
Order

630
37:49.530 --> 37:50.670
all regiments to stand by

631
37:50.670 --> 37:52.600
and be ready for battle at any time.

632
37:52.780 --> 37:54.240
You've had a hard journey.

633
37:55.270 --> 37:56.220
Come, have some milk tea.

634
37:56.220 --> 37:57.270
Have some milk tea.

635
37:57.270 --> 37:58.060
Thank you.

636
37:59.860 --> 38:00.530
Comrade Jianying.

637
38:00.530 --> 38:01.460
Come in quickly.

638
38:01.690 --> 38:03.080
Guard, close the door.

639
38:04.180 --> 38:05.110
Long time no see.

640
38:10.160 --> 38:11.070
Comrades.

641
38:12.340 --> 38:14.130
I've called you all here today

642
38:14.490 --> 38:17.130
because there is an important matter to announce.

643
38:17.130 --> 38:19.060
Aren't we going to forage for food?

644
38:19.780 --> 38:21.710
We are not going to forage for food.

645
38:22.770 --> 38:25.130
Zhang Guotao is openly causing a split

646
38:25.260 --> 38:27.190
and wants to lead the troops south.

647
38:30.040 --> 38:31.670
Now the Central Committee has decided

648
38:31.670 --> 38:33.370
to lead the 1st Front Army north alone.

649
38:33.370 --> 38:34.450
Tell me,

650
38:35.170 --> 38:35.970
what should we do?

651
38:35.970 --> 38:36.990
We will follow the Central Committee.

652
38:36.990 --> 38:37.830
I will listen to the Central Committee.

653
38:37.830 --> 38:38.520
We'll listen to the Central Committee.

654
38:38.520 --> 38:41.050
Yes, we all firmly follow the Central Committee.

655
38:41.050 --> 38:41.900
Good.

656
38:42.900 --> 38:43.820
In that case,

657
38:43.840 --> 38:45.060
please follow my instructions.

658
38:45.060 --> 38:46.540
After you all go back,

659
38:46.620 --> 38:48.490
immediately organize the comrades in your units

660
38:48.490 --> 38:49.590
and get ready to depart.

661
38:49.590 --> 38:51.150
We'll set out

662
38:51.840 --> 38:53.420
at exactly 2:00 a.m. today for Axi

663
38:53.420 --> 38:54.320
to join the Central Committee.

664
38:54.320 --> 38:55.110
Yes.

665
38:55.720 --> 38:57.450
Now synchronize your watches.

666
38:59.990 --> 39:02.720
It is now 8:35 p.m..

667
39:04.730 --> 39:07.130
Comrades, I wish you all the best.

668
40:07.950 --> 40:08.800
You're back.

669
40:10.380 --> 40:11.260
Yes.

670
40:17.270 --> 40:18.740
I'm heading out to gather grain tonight,

671
40:18.740 --> 40:20.340
so I won't say goodbye to you.

672
40:20.340 --> 40:20.780
Okay.

673
40:21.850 --> 40:22.670
Thanks for your hard work.

674
40:22.670 --> 40:23.870
I'll rest for a while.

675
40:28.950 --> 40:30.030
It's getting late.

676
40:30.050 --> 40:31.150
Let's all rest.

677
41:44.130 --> 41:44.990
What time is it?

678
41:47.940 --> 41:48.970
Half past nine.
